The complex-array absolute-value arithmetic in complex_math64.py adapts the
NumPy 1.26.4 ASIMD ufunc operation order from:
https://github.com/numpy/numpy/blob/v1.26.4/numpy/core/src/umath/loops_unary_complex.dispatch.c.src
Copyright (c) NumPy Developers. The NumPy license is retained in NumPy-LICENSE.

The separate array complex multiplication helpers adapt NumPy 1.26.4's
ASIMD multiply-add/subtract operation order from:
https://github.com/numpy/numpy/blob/v1.26.4/numpy/core/src/umath/loops_arithm_fp.dispatch.c.src
Scalar multiplication and products inside complex power retain their
distinct installed scalar operation order. Complex destination integer
casts preserve the installed NumPy cast-loop instruction widths/tails.

The complex arithmetic/ordering policies are compared with NumPy 1.26.4's
loops.c.src and npy_math_complex.c.src. The FreeBSD-derived complex-math source
license is retained in NumPy-complex-LICENSE.

The complex sin/cos/sinh/cosh, exp and sqrt component graphs are locally
authored semantic ports of the installed Apple ARM64 libsystem_m behavior,
reusing the existing qualified real arithmetic providers. They are not copies
of NumPy's alternative C99 fallback function bodies. Retained symbol bytes and
disassembly in the development evidence identify the reference target.
